course: dictionary
lesson: 8151
title: Latin words in English
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Requiescat is not ordinary English. It is a Latin word, and you may meet it on old gravestones or in church. It means «may he or she rest».
explain: The example says «Rest in Peace», RIP, comes from the Latin «Requiescat in pace», an old Christian prayer. RIP is the short form we write now, and we read it as «rest in peace».
explain: Look at the clues around the word. It sits next to «in pace», and the English words «Rest in Peace» match it, so you can work out the meaning even though the word is unfamiliar.
fact: Requiescat means «may he or she rest».
fact: «Requiescat in pace» means «may he or she rest in peace».
fact: Latin is an old language, and it is not the English you speak every day.
fact: The phrase is a prayer said for a person who has died.
fact: RIP is the short form of «Requiescat in pace», and we read it as «rest in peace».
exercise: What does requiescat mean? | Good morning to everyone | Goodbye until tomorrow | *May he or she rest | Let us sing loudly
exercise: RIP is a short form of which Latin words? | Run in parks | *Requiescat in pace | Rise in power | Red in peace
exercise: Which phrase is Latin and not everyday English? | Said for a person who has died | *Requiescat in pace | Old Christian prayer | Rest in Peace
test: On an old gravestone you read «Requiescat in pace». What does it mean? | *May he or she rest in peace | Happy birthday | Keep this place clean | Please come inside
test: Why might you see RIP on a gravestone? | It is the name of a church | It means the person was very tall | It is a number on the grave | *It is the short form of a Latin prayer meaning rest in peace
exam: The word requiescat comes from which language, and what does it mean? | English, meaning sleep well | Greek, meaning very loud | French, meaning come here | *Latin, meaning may he or she rest
